{
  "slug": "de-moivre-oq-03-oq-02",
  "title": "Riemann surface structure of z^(p/q)",
  "phase": "OBSERVE",
  "status": "active",
  "tier": "B",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "For coprime p, q (q >= 1), formalize the Riemann surface X = {(z,w) in C* x C : w^q = z^p} with projection pi(z,w)=z: pi is a q-sheeted holomorphic covering of C*, the deck/monodromy group is cyclic of order q generated by sigma(z,w) = (z, e^{2*pi*i*p/q} w), the origin is the unique branch point, and the compactified/normalized curve w^q = z^p is rational (genus 0) for gcd(p,q)=1.",
    "plain": "The map z -> z^(p/q) is multivalued: taking a q-th root gives q distinct answers. Instead of choosing a branch cut, one glues q copies of the punctured plane into a single connected Riemann surface on which z^(p/q) is single-valued. This problem formalizes that surface and its structure: a q-sheeted branched covering of C*, cyclic monodromy of order q that permutes the roots as z loops around 0, a single branch point at the origin, and the identification of the surface with the algebraic curve w^q = z^p.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Upgrades the pointwise fiber enumeration of the source entry (De Moivre OQ-03) to the global geometric object explaining why there are q roots and how they interconvert.",
      "It is the canonical first example of Riemann surface theory (branch points, monodromy, multivalued algebraic functions), an area essentially absent from Mathlib."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "De Moivre OQ-03 (verified gallery entry): the q roots zeta_k = exp(i(p*theta + 2*pi*k)/q) are enumerated, distinct, factor as zeta_k = zeta_0 * omega_k, and match Complex.cpow on the principal branch.",
      "Classically settled: the q-sheeted branched cover, cyclic monodromy Z/qZ, and rationality of w^q = z^p for gcd(p,q)=1 are standard (Forster, Miranda, Needham).",
      "Mathlib has cyclic roots-of-unity structure mu_q (IsPrimitiveRoot, Complex.isPrimitiveRoot_exp) and Kummer extension theory."
    ],
    "open": [
      "A Lean formalization of X = {w^q = z^p} as a covering space of C* with fibers of size q.",
      "A formal cyclic monodromy/deck group of order q with explicit generator (z,w) -> (z, omega^p w).",
      "Formal identification of the origin as the unique branch point and the genus-0/rationality conclusion for gcd(p,q)=1."
    ],
    "goal": "Core scope: define X over C*, prove each fiber has exactly q points (transporting OQ-03 enumeration/distinctness), define sigma(z,w)=(z, omega^p w), and prove <sigma> is cyclic of order q acting simply transitively on fibers (using gcd(p,q)=1). The full complex-manifold/covering topology and the compactification/genus statement are follow-on, out-of-initial-scope work."
  },
